t the router accuracy from plan-002 (58%) aligns with plan-003's eval results (60%), confirming plan-003's overall score feeds into plan-004, and validating that the 2-way classification (63%) outperforms 3-way (58%) as expected, plus within-domain chemistry (62%) exceeds the overall 3-way baseline.\n\nLet me tally up the GPU hours: 35 + 6 + 14 + 9 + 1.5 + 7 + 2.5 + 11 + 4 equals 90 hours against a 103-hour budget, so I'm at 87% utilization which is solid. I should also double-check that the task_types_with_significant_gain count of 4 falls within the [3,7] tier range for plan-003, and note that 2 task types show internal performance exceeding simulated performance.\n\nNow I'm looking at where SimGate actually underperforms compared to the internal baseline—find-living and find-nonliving both show a 2-point gap where the router's unnecessary deterministic routing causes issues. I'm also verifying the catastrophic failure reduction: internal sits at 19.7%, SimGate brings it down to 13.0%, which is a 34% improvement and fits the [20,40] target range. Always-deterministic achieves 68% reduction, so SimGate's gains are meaningful but more modest.\n\nI've confirmed all 10 plan items are accounted for in the imagined experiments, so I'm ready to format the final YAML response.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10575},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38cf3b9f-177b-4d21-8c68-b4701e84ba77","uuid":"4d2b765b-c449-4cf1-b803-668b93a9750b"}
